terms='''<div class="wrap"><article class="legal"><div class="eyebrow">Fresh Destination</div><h1>Terms & Conditions</h1><p>These terms apply to bookings made through Fresh Destination for airport transfers and chauffeur services.</p><h2>1. Booking & Payment</h2><p>A booking is confirmed only after payment requirements are satisfied and confirmation is issued. Prices may differ by city, date, vehicle class, service hours and supplier availability.</p><h2>2. Vehicle Assignment</h2><p>Vehicle images and models shown are examples. The exact make, model, year, colour and configuration may vary. A comparable vehicle class may be supplied based on availability.</p><h2>3. Passenger & Luggage Limits</h2><p>Passengers must select a vehicle suitable for the number of travellers and luggage. Oversized or excess luggage must be declared before travel.</p><h2>4. Airport Pickup</h2><p>Customers must provide correct flight details. Reasonable waiting time may be included; additional waiting may incur charges according to the booking conditions.</p><h2>5. Chauffeur by Day</h2><p>Daily services are sold for the booked number of service hours. Extra time, parking, tolls, attractions, long-distance surcharges or driver accommodation may be charged separately where applicable.</p><h2>6. Local Providers</h2><p>Services may be fulfilled by licensed local transport providers in Australia, Japan or South Korea. Fresh Destination coordinates the booking and customer experience.</p><h2>7. Changes</h2><p>Changes are subject to provider availability and may result in a fare adjustment.</p><h2>8. Conduct & Safety</h2><p>Passengers must follow reasonable driver safety instructions and applicable local laws. Smoking or illegal activity is not permitted in vehicles.</p><h2>9. Liability</h2><p>Fresh Destination and its providers are not responsible for delays caused by traffic, weather, road closures, airport disruption or events outside reasonable control.</p><h2>10. Contact</h2><p>For booking support, contact Fresh Destination using the support details shown on your booking confirmation.</p></article></div>'''
(base/'terms.html').write_text(page('Terms & Conditions',terms))

cancel='''<div class="wrap"><article class="legal"><div class="eyebrow">Fresh Destination</div><h1>Cancellation Policy</h1><p>Cancellation and refund eligibility depends on how far in advance the booking is cancelled and on supplier-specific conditions displayed at checkout.</p><h2>Customer Cancellation</h2><ul><li>More than 72 hours before service: normally eligible for the highest available refund, less non-refundable payment or supplier charges where disclosed.</li><li>24–72 hours before service: partial cancellation charges may apply.</li><li>Less than 24 hours before service or no-show: booking may be non-refundable.</li></ul><h2>Flight Delays</h2><p>Where flight monitoring is included, the provider will make reasonable efforts to adjust pickup time. Significant changes may require reconfirmation.</p><h2>Provider Cancellation</h2><p>If a confirmed provider cannot perform the service, Fresh Destination will attempt to arrange a suitable replacement. If no replacement can be arranged, the affected service will be refunded.</p><h2>Changes to Bookings</h2><p>Date, pickup time, route, passenger count or vehicle changes are subject to availability and may change the price.</p><h2>Refund Timing</h2><p>Approved refunds are returned to the original payment method. Bank and card processing times vary.</p><h2>How to Cancel</h2><p>Use the booking management link in your confirmation email or contact Fresh Destination support and quote your booking reference.</p></article></div>'''
(base/'cancellation.html').write_text(page('Cancellation Policy',cancel))

